## 📋 FRONTMATTER REQUIREMENTS

### **Frontmatter vaaditaan: title, description, date (ISO), author, tags[], locale, heroImage** (Frontmatter required: title, description, date (ISO), author, tags[], locale, heroImage)

### **Required Frontmatter Structure**
```yaml
---
title: "Communication ecosystem for professional service companies"
description: "Learn how to build a comprehensive communication strategy that transforms your professional service company's communication into a competitive advantage."
date: "2024-01-15T10:00:00Z"
author: "Lyyli Team"
tags: ["communication", "professional-services", "strategy", "ai"]
locale: "en"
heroImage: "/images/blog/communication-ecosystem-hero.jpg"
---
```

### **Frontmatter Validation**
```typescript
// lib/blog/validateFrontmatter.ts
interface BlogFrontmatter {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  date: string; // ISO format
  author: string;
  tags: string[];
  locale: 'en' | 'fi';
  heroImage: string;
}

export function validateFrontmatter(frontmatter: any): BlogFrontmatter {
  const required = ['title', 'description', 'date', 'author', 'tags', 'locale', 'heroImage'];
  const missing = required.filter(field => !frontmatter[field]);
  
  if (missing.length > 0) {
    throw new Error(`Missing required frontmatter fields: ${missing.join(', ')}`);
  }
  
  // Validate date format
  if (!isValidISOString(frontmatter.date)) {
    throw new Error('Date must be in ISO format');
  }
  
  // Validate locale
  if (!['en', 'fi'].includes(frontmatter.locale)) {
    throw new Error('Locale must be "en" or "fi"');
  }
  
  // Validate tags array
  if (!Array.isArray(frontmatter.tags) || frontmatter.tags.length === 0) {
    throw new Error('Tags must be a non-empty array');
  }
  
  return frontmatter as BlogFrontmatter;
}

function isValidISOString(dateString: string): boolean {
  const date = new Date(dateString);
  return date instanceof Date && !isNaN(date.getTime());
}
```

## 🔗 SLUG GENERATION

### **Slugit = tiedostonimi (pienet kirjaimet, ei välilyöntejä)** (Slugs = filename (lowercase, no spaces))

### **Slug Rules**
- **File-based**: Slug matches the filename exactly
- **Lowercase**: All characters converted to lowercase
- **No Spaces**: Spaces replaced with hyphens
- **No Special Characters**: Remove or replace special characters

### **Slug Examples**
```typescript
// File: communication-ecosystem.mdx
// Slug: /blog/communication-ecosystem

// File: ai-communication-expert-teams.mdx
// Slug: /blog/ai-communication-expert-teams

// File: sisaisen-viestinnan-sudenkuopat.mdx
// Slug: /fi/blog/sisaisen-viestinnan-sudenkuopat
```

### **Slug Implementation**
```typescript
// lib/blog/getSlug.ts
export function getSlug(filename: string): string {
  // Remove .mdx extension
  const nameWithoutExt = filename.replace(/\.mdx$/, '');
  
  // Convert to lowercase and replace spaces with hyphens
  return nameWithoutExt.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '-');
}

// Usage in blog listing
export function getBlogPosts() {
  const posts = fs.readdirSync(blogDirectory);
  
  return posts.map(filename => {
    const slug = getSlug(filename);
    const fullPath = path.join(blogDirectory, filename);
    const source = fs.readFileSync(fullPath, 'utf8');
    const { data } = matter(source);
    
    return {
      slug,
      frontmatter: data,
      content: source
    };
  });
}
```

